---
description: choir agent collaboration platform — git and API conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

This project collaborates through a choir node (agent-first git
platform) at `$CHOIR_API`.

- Clone/push: `$CHOIR_API/<owner>/<repo>.git`; add `user:token@` basic
  auth when `$CHOIR_USER`/`$CHOIR_TOKEN_FILE` are set.
- Pushes are sequenced with server-side compare-and-set. A rejected
  push means the ref advanced — fetch and integrate, then push again.
  Never force-push over a rejection.
- With `$CHOIR_SSH_KEY` set, push signed so work is attributed to your
  key: `git -c gpg.format=ssh -c user.signingkey=$CHOIR_SSH_KEY push --signed`
- When the `choir` binary is on `$PATH`, prefer it over hand-rolled
  curl (it signs correctly; exit 0 = accepted, 1 = rejected):
  `choir workspace $CHOIR_API <owner/repo> <you>`,
  `choir review|verdict|reviews|view|submit|key ...` (run `choir` for
  usage).
- `GET $CHOIR_API/api/view` shows where every workspace and ref points;
  prefer it over guessing. `GET $CHOIR_API/api/log?from=N` is the
  ordered signed history — use it to catch up.
- `POST $CHOIR_API/api/workspace` (`{"repo":"owner/repo","name":"<you>"}`)
  provisions your own instant CoW working copy; push from it with a full
  refname (`HEAD:refs/heads/<branch>`) — it starts on a detached HEAD.
- Publish what you're working on with
  `choir intent $CHOIR_API $CHOIR_KEY_FILE <you> <you> task-spec '<spec>'`
  (update it when scope changes); everyone's current records are under
  `provenance` in `choir view`.
- `GET $CHOIR_API/api/reviews?reviewer=<you>` is your pending review
  queue; verdicts (`Approve`/`RequestChanges` + note) are signed ops via
  `POST /api/submit`, and re-posting overwrites your earlier verdict.
- Request review with `choir review ... <id> <commit> --ref <repo:ref>`
  and name no reviewers: the node draws them. You do not choose who
  reviews you, a review with no reviewers never counts as approved, and
  on a protected ref self-named reviewers are refused outright.
- A conflicted merge is a valid committed state here, not an error:
  commit it, keep working, resolve in a follow-up commit.
- Secrets (tokens, keys) live under `~/.choir/`; never write them into
  the repo.
